{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_plans_mvp_review_final_summary_r3", "label": "REVIEW-FINAL-summary-r3.md", "file_type": "document", "rationale": "MVP acceptance walk run 3 (2026-11-14) summary: verdict, checklist rows, what the phase changed, decisions, open findings, latent items, gaps and honesty notes. Lens files untracked: REVIEW-FINAL-organiser-r3.md, -practitioner-r3.md, -roles-r3.md, -gapfill-r3.md.", "source_file": "docs/plans/mvp/REVIEW-FINAL-summary-r3.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_plans_mvp_review_final_summary_r3_verdict", "label": "Walk r3 verdict: MVP spine closed on the working tree", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Spine is create, publish, register, check in, record. Live walk found no BLOCKER and no new MAJOR; every spine row has an executed result. Three conditions, each Ivan's: M1 stays open; nothing is committed (clean-worktree gate chain NOT RUN); Seoul has none of the five migrations.", "source_file": "docs/plans/mvp/REVIEW-FINAL-summary-r3.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_plans_mvp_review_final_summary_r3_walk_setup", "label": "Walk r3 setup: :3100, review mode off, local stack", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Server :3100, EVENTAR_REVIEW_MODE=false (signed-out /events/new gave 307 to /login), local stack only, Seoul untouched. Walk and gates ran on 1f3d958 plus uncommitted changes. Evidence tags: [X] executed, [R] read in code, [I] inferred; a row without [X] is not a pass.", "source_file": "docs/plans/mvp/REVIEW-FINAL-summary-r3.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_plans_mvp_review_final_summary_r3_f1_speaker_checkins_window", "label": "F1 MINOR: no DB-level window gate on speaker_checkins", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Only the Server Action refuses. Any authenticated member of the organisation can INSERT directly, 5 hours before the window opened in the walk. Recommend yes: a small trigger like the attendee one; cost one migration and one test. Not a regression of this phase.", "source_file": "docs/plans/mvp/REVIEW-FINAL-summary-r3.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_plans_mvp_review_final_summary_r3_m1_consent_copy_404", "label": "M1 MAJOR: consent copy names Terms and Privacy pages that 404", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "The consent step says Terms and Privacy will be published before launch; /terms, /privacy, /legal/terms and /legal/privacy all return 404. Predates this phase. Recommend wait because the brief parked legal; rewording is the smaller fix if the strict bar is wanted. By the skill's strict bar one open MAJOR keeps done open.", "source_file": "docs/plans/mvp/REVIEW-FINAL-summary-r3.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_plans_mvp_review_final_summary_r3_f2_roster_stale", "label": "F2 MINOR: check-in roster stale after Enter-code check-in", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Roster did not update until reload. Ruled: S4 is not the cause. A confirmed staff probe subscribed to registrations, checked in via the real mark_attended path, the event arrived, credit_ledger 920 before and after. The browser pane was not re-walked, so the cause in the pane is unproven.", "source_file": "docs/plans/mvp/REVIEW-FINAL-summary-r3.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_plans_mvp_review_final_summary_r3_row_o3_agenda", "label": "Row O3 agenda, no silent loss: PASS", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "3 blocks in, 3 out, ids stable across saves (S6), block removed cleanly, window refusal reads in plain words (S5).", "source_file": "docs/plans/mvp/REVIEW-FINAL-summary-r3.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_plans_mvp_review_final_summary_r3_row_o4_publish_gate", "label": "Row O4 publish gate: PASS", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Creator and non-creator admin: confirm dialog, published_at set, created_by unchanged. A member publishes only their own draft.", "source_file": "docs/plans/mvp/REVIEW-FINAL-summary-r3.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_plans_mvp_review_final_summary_r3_row_o7_checkin_window", "label": "Row O7 check-in only inside the window: PASS", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Tested before, inside, after and on a stale page; server refusal text read. The DB-level speaker gate is F1.", "source_file": "docs/plans/mvp/REVIEW-FINAL-summary-r3.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_plans_mvp_review_final_summary_r3_row_o8_walk_in", "label": "Row O8 walk-in, no staff identity: PASS", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "source=walk_in, user_id and profile_snapshot NULL, no staff id in any attendee column.", "source_file": "docs/plans/mvp/REVIEW-FINAL-summary-r3.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_plans_mvp_review_final_summary_r3_row_o9_post_event", "label": "Row O9 post-event path: PARTIAL", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "The 2-click path passes; the registrants CSV was not exported live.", "source_file": "docs/plans/mvp/REVIEW-FINAL-summary-r3.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_plans_mvp_review_final_summary_r3_row_a2_signup_consent", "label": "Row A2 sign-up, wizard, consent: PASS", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Cold start from /login (G1) lands on /account/registrations. Both consent rows written by the wizard. M1 applies.", "source_file": "docs/plans/mvp/REVIEW-FINAL-summary-r3.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_plans_mvp_review_final_summary_r3_row_roles_member_body", "label": "Rows ux-member R3a to R3g and ux-body R4: PASS", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Member lands on Events, creates and publishes own draft; another's draft is read-only; direct REST write refused 42501 not_event_writer; Enter-code check-in as a member is creator only. Body role is read-only everywhere, REST write refused 42501, publish_event refused.", "source_file": "docs/plans/mvp/REVIEW-FINAL-summary-r3.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_plans_mvp_review_final_summary_r3_row_s1_consent_write", "label": "Row S1 consent write path: PASS", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Wizard still writes both rows. Direct write refused 42501 (RLS matrix).", "source_file": "docs/plans/mvp/REVIEW-FINAL-summary-r3.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_plans_mvp_review_final_summary_r3_row_s2_s3", "label": "Rows S2 and S3: PASS", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "S2: curl -I on the running server plus tests/nextConfigHeaders.test.ts (orchestrator-run, no lens file). S3: pnpm why zod shows 4.6.7; pnpm audit --prod has no zod row.", "source_file": "docs/plans/mvp/REVIEW-FINAL-summary-r3.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_plans_mvp_review_final_summary_r3_row_s4_confirmed_email", "label": "Row S4 confirmed email: PASS (DB-claims only)", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "GoTrue refuses the unconfirmed sign-in first, so no authenticated REST call can exist. Forged claims in psql see 0 rows; a confirmed control sees 9 / 310 / true. Realtime for a confirmed staff user still works (probe, see F2).", "source_file": "docs/plans/mvp/REVIEW-FINAL-summary-r3.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_plans_mvp_review_final_summary_r3_row_s5_window", "label": "Row S5 block inside window: PASS", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Enforced at three layers: form flag, action refusal, DB trigger. DB unchanged after the refusal.", "source_file": "docs/plans/mvp/REVIEW-FINAL-summary-r3.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_plans_mvp_review_final_summary_r3_row_s7_csv", "label": "Row S7 CSV formula guard: PASS (unit only)", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "lib/csv.test.ts 31 of 31. Registrants, attendance, College and participants exports route through buildCsv (read in code). Live export NOT RUN.", "source_file": "docs/plans/mvp/REVIEW-FINAL-summary-r3.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_plans_mvp_review_final_summary_r3_row_s8_capacity", "label": "Row S8 capacity: PASS", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Review row says staff walk-in refused; public form refused on a full event; a row inserted mid-form gave 'This event is at capacity.' and the count stayed 1; parallel clicks covered by the RLS test. Tension: the handoff says S8 leaves walk-ins exempt, and the files do not reconcile this with 'staff walk-in refused'.", "source_file": "docs/plans/mvp/REVIEW-FINAL-summary-r3.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_plans_mvp_review_final_summary_r3_gates_pass", "label": "Gates that pass: tsc, eslint, ui-colours, test:rls, next build", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "tsc exit 0; eslint 0 errors, 11 warnings; check:ui-colours clean; pnpm test:rls two stages 50 files / 483 tests then 5 files / 57 tests; next build exit 0 on a dirty tree. Last full chain was gate3.out; only docs changed after it.", "source_file": "docs/plans/mvp/REVIEW-FINAL-summary-r3.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_plans_mvp_review_final_summary_r3_gate_ui_primitives", "label": "Gate check:ui-primitives FAIL (pre-existing, 4 hits)", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "None in a file touched this phase: ProfileClient.tsx:510, OrgOnboardingClient.tsx:120 and :142, MultiBodyAccreditationWizard.tsx:245. Same four as r2.", "source_file": "docs/plans/mvp/REVIEW-FINAL-summary-r3.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_plans_mvp_review_final_summary_r3_gate_vitest", "label": "Gate vitest plain run: 2832 of 2833, not a clean run", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "The one failure is a DDL deadlock in registrations_link_immutability (error: deadlock detected). That file runs in the serial stage and passes alone: 5 files, 87 tests, re-run today.", "source_file": "docs/plans/mvp/REVIEW-FINAL-summary-r3.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_plans_mvp_review_final_summary_r3_gate_clean_worktree", "label": "Gate chain on a clean worktree at a final HEAD: NOT RUN", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Nothing is committed. It runs after Ivan gives the commit go (eventar-static-gates). The MVP-done declaration becomes final only when it passes and Ivan rules on M1.", "source_file": "docs/plans/mvp/REVIEW-FINAL-summary-r3.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_plans_mvp_review_final_summary_r3_latent_export_analytics_csv", "label": "Latent: ExportAnalyticsCsv.tsx has its own esc, no formula guard", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "components/analytics/ExportAnalyticsCsv.tsx builds CSV with its own esc. Its cells are fixed survey option labels today, so it is not exploitable now. Fold into buildCsv when next touched.", "source_file": "docs/plans/mvp/REVIEW-FINAL-summary-r3.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_plans_mvp_review_final_summary_r3_latent_events_home_csvescape", "label": "Latent: EventsHome.tsx duplicate csvEscape", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "components/dashboard/EventsHome.tsx keeps a duplicate csvEscape. It neutralises formulas but lacks the signed-number exception.", "source_file": "docs/plans/mvp/REVIEW-FINAL-summary-r3.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_plans_mvp_review_final_summary_r3_latent_walk_window_sh", "label": "Latent: scripts/walk-window.sh fails on events with agenda blocks", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "The S5 trigger blocks the plain update events the helper runs. The guard works; the helper needs the delete and re-insert shape.", "source_file": "docs/plans/mvp/REVIEW-FINAL-summary-r3.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_plans_mvp_review_final_summary_r3_latent_lockfile", "label": "Latent: pnpm update zod re-resolved transitives", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "lightningcss 1.33.0, postcss 8.5.33, tinyglobby 0.2.17, tslib 2.9.1, @napi-rs/wasm-runtime, rolldown pluginutils. Every gate passes on it. Review the lockfile diff at commit time.", "source_file": "docs/plans/mvp/REVIEW-FINAL-summary-r3.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_plans_mvp_review_final_summary_r3_latent_pnpm_audit", "label": "Latent: pnpm audit --prod lists 6 advisories", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "browserslist, source-map-js, @babel/core, baseline-browser-mapping, deepmerge. None is zod; all are build-tool transitives under next and @react-email. Not triaged.", "source_file": "docs/plans/mvp/REVIEW-FINAL-summary-r3.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_plans_mvp_review_final_summary_r3_latent_cancelled_seat", "label": "Latent: cancelled registration may still hold a seat", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "A cancelled registration may still hold a seat toward capacity. Not walked.", "source_file": "docs/plans/mvp/REVIEW-FINAL-summary-r3.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_plans_mvp_review_final_summary_r3_latent_csv_header", "label": "Latent: registrants CSV Start header mislabelled", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "The registrants CSV header Start ...+00:00 (Asia/Hong_Kong) is mislabelled. Parked in the brief.", "source_file": "docs/plans/mvp/REVIEW-FINAL-summary-r3.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_plans_mvp_review_final_summary_r3_minor_events_home_300", "label": "MINOR: Events home counts under-count past 300 events", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Under-count when the organisation has more than 300 events (test data has 533). One generic footer line warns. Source: roles lens.", "source_file": "docs/plans/mvp/REVIEW-FINAL-summary-r3.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_plans_mvp_review_final_summary_r3_minor_member_draft", "label": "MINOR: member on another's draft sees mixed reasons", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "The ownership reason shows next to an unrelated accreditation sentence. The disabled Save has no aria-describedby.", "source_file": "docs/plans/mvp/REVIEW-FINAL-summary-r3.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_plans_mvp_review_final_summary_r3_minor_organiser_door", "label": "MINOR: practitioner at the organiser door sees an error-styled page", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Shown after a valid link. Recovery exists. Source: gapfill lens.", "source_file": "docs/plans/mvp/REVIEW-FINAL-summary-r3.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_plans_mvp_review_final_summary_r3_minor_public_registration", "label": "MINOR: public registration copy gaps", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Confirmation tells a signed-in user this browser tab is their proof. The capacity race message has no next step. Register is greyed for a whitespace-only name with no reason.", "source_file": "docs/plans/mvp/REVIEW-FINAL-summary-r3.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_plans_mvp_review_final_summary_r3_gaps_not_run", "label": "Gaps: steps not run", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "O2 Drafts-tab title; O9 registrants CSV file and a live S7 export; O3 add-a-block-past-the-end; /account/check-in and /account/record; invalid-email and duplicate-registration wrong turns; Enter-code check-in as a non-creator member; self-serve check-in window (off by default); F2 in the browser pane. R6 was covered by G1 instead.", "source_file": "docs/plans/mvp/REVIEW-FINAL-summary-r3.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_plans_mvp_review_final_summary_r3_honesty_notes", "label": "Honesty notes", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Walk ran on the uncommitted tree; source unchanged after gate3.out. No screenshots on disk; evidence is page text and DB read-backs. Four lenses hit call caps; unreached steps are not counted as passes. credit_ledger grew from 889 to 920 rows locally. The Realtime probe left a fixture once (a participation_evidence row blocked its delete); removed, leftover count 0. Expected residue is audit_events (permanent by Hard Rule 11).", "source_file": "docs/plans/mvp/REVIEW-FINAL-summary-r3.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_plans_mvp_review_final_summary_r3_phase_protocol", "label": "Phase protocol: dev review, separate user review, backtest", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "The two reviews ran as separate agents before the fix wave; their findings are fixed test-first. Hand-backs are not saved as files. The walk with its DB read-backs is the backtest.", "source_file": "docs/plans/mvp/REVIEW-FINAL-summary-r3.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_plans_mvp_review_final_summary_r3", "target": "docs_plans_mvp_review_final_summary_r3_verdict", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/plans/mvp/REVIEW-FINAL-summary-r3.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_plans_mvp_review_final_summary_r3", "target": "docs_plans_mvp_review_final_summary_r3_walk_setup", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/plans/mvp/REVIEW-FINAL-summary-r3.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_plans_mvp_review_final_summary_r3", "target": "docs_plans_mvp_review_final_summary_r3_f1_speaker_checkins_window", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/plans/mvp/REVIEW-FINAL-summary-r3.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_plans_mvp_review_final_summary_r3", "target": "docs_plans_mvp_review_final_summary_r3_m1_consent_copy_404", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": 